From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: fix: mark leaked serial device observation as dangling on Windows

With dangling raw_ptr checks enabled, the browser process fails
CheckDanglingRawPtrBufferEmpty() at exit on Windows after any page has
used navigator.serial.

SerialDeviceEnumeratorWin::UiThreadHelper observes the
DeviceMonitorWin for GUID_DEVINTERFACE_COMPORT through a
base::ScopedObservation, which holds a raw_ptr to it. The helper is
owned through SerialDeviceEnumeratorWin by SerialPortManagerImpl, which
DeviceService keeps in a SequenceBound on a ThreadPool sequence.
content binds DeviceService in the UI thread's SequenceLocalStorage, so
it is destroyed in BrowserTaskExecutor::Shutdown(), after
ThreadPoolInstance::Shutdown(). The task that would delete the
SerialPortManagerImpl is dropped, and the enumerator and helper are
leaked with the observation still active. AtExitManager then deletes
DeviceMonitorMessageWindow and its DeviceMonitorWin instances, leaving
the observation's raw_ptr dangling.

The pointer is never used after that, so mark the observation
LeakedDanglingUntriaged, as base::ScopedObservation provides for
observations that are known to leak (crbug.com/493572976).
HidServiceWin and UsbServiceWin are not affected because DeviceService
owns them directly on the UI thread and destroys them before AtExit.

diff --git a/services/device/serial/serial_device_enumerator_win.cc b/services/device/serial/serial_device_enumerator_win.cc
index 62c92e4dde2d092b2d25a879d600093149b587f3..f132042de2f1885b07b009739910a1c6128c0a5f 100644
--- a/services/device/serial/serial_device_enumerator_win.cc
+++ b/services/device/serial/serial_device_enumerator_win.cc
@@ -494,7 +494,13 @@ class SerialDeviceEnumeratorWin::UiThreadHelper
   base::WeakPtr<SerialDeviceEnumeratorWin> enumerator_;
   scoped_refptr<base::SequencedTaskRunner> task_runner_;
 
-  base::ScopedObservation<DeviceMonitorWin, DeviceMonitorWin::Observer>
+  // The browser destroys DeviceService after the ThreadPool has shut down, so
+  // the SerialPortManagerImpl that owns the enumerator, and in turn this
+  // helper, is leaked with the observation still active. The DeviceMonitorWin
+  // is then deleted by an AtExitManager callback, leaving this pointer
+  // dangling but never used.
+  base::ScopedObservation<DeviceMonitorWin,
+                          DeviceMonitorWin::Observer>::LeakedDanglingUntriaged
       device_observation_{this};
 };
 
